+# CodeModule_CONTRACT.md
+
+Status: SPEC (PLAN‑ONLY) — API contract for CodeModule implementations
+Source of truth: derived from CHAT_PLAN.md ("CodeModule — scelte di contratto")
+
+Purpose
+- Define the public API and response schema that every normative CodeModule (e.g. NTC2018) must implement.
+- No implementation details here — only interface, expected inputs/outputs and error semantics.
+
+Interface (public)
+- available_checks() -> list[str]
+  - returns the identifiers of checks exposed by the module
+
+- available_templates() -> list[str]
+  - returns named input templates (useful for GUI template picker)
+
+- validate_input(check_id: str, payload: dict) -> ValidationResult
+  - contract: must only validate schema/units/presence of required fields (no normative calculation)
+  - ValidationResult: { valid: bool, errors: list[str] }
+
+- run_check(check_id: str, payload: dict) -> VerificationResultItem
+  - contract: synchronous call that returns a single VerificationResultItem (see schema below)
+  - implementation MUST NOT mutate payload
+  - implementation MUST populate norm_references[] and trace.run_id
+
+VerificationResultItem (response schema) — required fields
+- id: string (unique per check instance)
+- reference: { norma: str, paragrafo?: str, capitolo?: str }
+- capitolo_ntc: enum {CAP_4, CAP_7, ...} (when applicable)
+- demand: numeric | null (Ed-like)
+- capacity: numeric | null (Rd-like)
+- ratio: numeric | null (source‑of‑truth; GUI only formats)
+- status: enum { OK, NOT_OK, NOT_APPLICABLE, WARNING }
+- utilisation: numeric (0..1) | null
+- steps: list[str] (human‑readable steps, no formula derivation in GUI)
+- norm_references: list[ { norm: str, clause?: str, href?: str } ]  — MUST be present (or TODO tag)
+- messages: list[str] (warnings/errors)
+- sle: optional object (serviceability outputs)
+- metadata: { timestamp: ISO8601, solver_version?: str, run_id: str, calculation_code_version?: str }
+
+Error handling
+- API calls should raise documented exceptions or return ValidationResult with errors.
+- run_check must never return partially computed numeric values without an explicit `status` and `messages` explaining the issue.
+
+Examples
+- TODO-CONTRACT-EXAMPLES — add example VerificationResult JSONs for OK / NOT_OK / NOT_APPLICABLE (required in CHAT_PLAN.md)
+
+Acceptance criteria for any CodeModule implementation
+- exposes checks via available_checks()
+- run_check returns VerificationResultItem consistent with schema above
+- every numeric result has corresponding norm_references[] entries (or explicit TODO)
+- trace.run_id always present in metadata
+
+Notes / Constraints
+- GUI layers are NOT allowed to perform any normative calculation — GUI must treat VerificationResultItem as source‑of‑truth.
+- Any normative formula or coefficient must be referenced to a normative source in norm_references[] or marked TODO.
+

