+# TEST_PLAN_NTC2018.md
+
+Status: SPEC (PLAN‑ONLY) — Golden cases & test strategy for NTC2018 modules
+Source: CHAT_PLAN.md — Testing, validation and documentation
+
+Objectives
+- Provide numerical golden fixtures, expected outcomes and tolerances for NTC2018 checks (including V_Rd,c) and for Secondary Elements templates.
+- Define coverage threshold for new normative modules (recommended >= 90%).
+
+General rules
+- All golden tests MUST reference a normative source (NTC2018 / EC2 / DM96 / official worked example).
+- If source is paywalled or missing, mark the fixture with TODO and a rationale.
+- Unit tests must be deterministic and small (single check).
+- Integration tests must validate end‑to‑end mapping: ProjectModel → VerificationEngine → CodeModule → ReportBuilder.
+
+Coverage target
+- New normative modules: target >= 90% coverage (documented in CI job)
+
+Golden fixtures (high level — details in SPEC files)
+- V_Rd,c (RC_SLU_VRDc_NoStirrups)
+  - Case A (PASS): geometry + material → expected V_Rd,c and utilisation (γ_c default = 1.5). Source: EN1992‑1‑1 §6.2 (or worked example). If NA, mark TODO.
+  - Case B (FAIL): same geometry, higher Ed.
+  - Case C (NOT_APPLICABLE): geometry outside applicability bounds.
+  - Case D (axial benefit): include σ_cp > 0.
+
+- Secondary elements (per template: Cantilever, Signage, Partition, Chimney)
+  - For each template: PASS / FAIL / NOT_APPLICABLE fixtures (3+ per template).
+  - All fixtures must document source (NTC2018 §7.2, EC1 for wind, DM96 where SLE referenced) — mark TODO if source unavailable.
+
+Integration tests (examples)
+- tests/integration/test_norm_switching.py — same model verified under NTC2018 and RD2229 yields VerificationResultItem with appropriate norm_references[].
+- tests/integration/test_gui_verification_flow.py — UI flow: select norm → create secondary → run checks → verify VerificationResultItem + run_id present.
+
+Test data hygiene
+- Store fixtures in tests/fixtures/ with a clear mapping to SPEC files.
+- Every test referring to a TODO fixture must assert TODO presence in test metadata (instead of numeric equality).
+
+Acceptance gates
+- All new checks must include at least 3 golden fixtures referenced in TEST_PLAN_NTC2018.md and linked in SPEC files.
+- CI must run the full test suite and satisfy coverage gates (post‑SPEC approval).
+

