+# SPEC_SecondaryElementSpec.md
+
+Status: SPEC (PLAN‑ONLY) — Secondary elements (NTC2018 §7.2 + fallback)
+Source: CHAT_PLAN.md (final approved SPEC)
+
+Summary
+- Defines the `SecondaryElementSpec` data contract, template models, GUI bindings and acceptance tests for secondary elements:
+  - CANTILEVER (mensola)
+  - SIGNAGE (insegna / pannello sospeso)
+  - PARTITION (tramezzo / partizione non portante)
+  - CHIMNEY (camino / comignolo)
+
+1. Data contract (SecondaryElementInput — required fields)
+- id: string
+- type: enum {CANTILEVER, SIGNAGE, PARTITION, CHIMNEY, OTHER}
+- geometry: { width_mm?, height_mm?, thickness_mm?, length_mm?, diameter_mm?, span_mm? }
+- material: { material_code: str, f_ck_MPa?: number, gamma_c?: number (default 1.5) }
+- attachments: list[{ position, anchor_type, embedment_depth_mm, stiffness }]
+- loads: { Gk:[], Qk:[], wind: {pressure, direction}, seismic: {a_g, importance}, accidental:[] }
+- boundary_conditions: { top_support, bottom_support, rotational_stiffness }
+- dynamic: optional { modal_mass, damping } (TODO — dynamic analysis reserved)
+- notes / user_flags
+- created_from_template: string
+
+2. Expected VerificationResultItem output (per check)
+- check_id (string)
+- status ∈ {OK, NOT_OK, NOT_APPLICABLE, WARNING}
+- utilisation (0..1) where applicable
+- value (numeric, optional)
+- steps[] (human‑readable, reference only)
+- norm_references[] (list of normative references or TODO)
+- messages[] (warnings / remediation hints)
+- required_followup[] (e.g., geotech, dynamic_analysis)
+- trace: { run_id: str, norm_references[] }
+
+3. Per‑template behavior (high level)
+- CANTILEVER (mensola)
+  - checks: secondary_cantilever_moment, secondary_cantilever_shear, secondary_cantilever_anchor, secondary_cantilever_deflection (SLE)
+  - applicability: small/medium spans typical for non‑primary elements (numeric limits = TODO)
+  - test fixtures: PASS / FAIL / NOT_APPLICABLE
+
+- SIGNAGE (insegna/pannello sospeso)
+  - checks: secondary_signage_anchor (anchor capacity by anchor), secondary_signage_serviceability (vibration/fatigue — TODO)
+  - applicability: dynamic amplification → TODO (may be NOT_APPLICABLE)
+  - examples: manufacturer ETA placeholders (TODO)
+
+- PARTITION (tramezzo)
+  - checks: secondary_partition_out_of_plane, secondary_partition_serviceability (SLE)
+  - applicability: large spans / special cladding → NOT_APPLICABLE (TODO numeric limits)
+
+- CHIMNEY (camino)
+  - checks: secondary_chimney_buckling, secondary_chimney_foundation (requires GeotechAdapter)
+  - applicability: tall/slender chimneys may REQUIRE_GEOTECH
+
+4. GUI bindings (mapping)
+- Editor fields map 1:1 to SecondaryElementInput keys.
+- `src/gui/secondary_elements/editor.py` must validate units and required fields, then persist to `ProjectModel.secondary_elements[]`.
+- `Run verification` → `VerificationEngine.run_check(check_id, SecondaryElementSpec)` (calculation_code chosen by norma selector)
+- Results panel shows VerificationResultItem.steps[], norm_references[], messages[] and includes trace.run_id
+- GUI must not compute normative values (ratio/capacity) — these are produced by core and displayed formatted (3 decimals)
+
+5. Storage / templates
+- Templates registry file: `config/codes/ntc2018/secondary_elements.jsoncode` (skeleton created)
+- Project model: add `secondary_elements[]` (documented in IMPLEMENTAZIONE_PERSISTENZA.md)
+
+6. Tests & acceptance
+- For each template provide 3 golden tests: PASS / FAIL / NOT_APPLICABLE
+- Each test must reference a normative source or be marked TODO
+- Acceptance: `CodeModule.available_checks()` exposes secondary_* check ids and GUI can run them producing VerificationResultItems with trace.run_id and norm_references[]
+
+7. Traceability & metadata (mandatory)
+- Every VerificationResultItem MUST include `trace.run_id` and `trace.norm_references[]`
+- GUI and ReportBuilder must surface run_id and norm_references[] in headers and detail panes
+
+8. TODO (explicit)
+- TODO-SE1: define numeric applicability limits (slenderness, embedment depths)
+- TODO-SE2: anchor capacity formulas / ETA references
+- TODO-SE3: SLE criteria (deflection / crack width limits)
+- TODO-SE4: wind coefficients / dynamic amplification (EC1 reference)
+- TODO-SE5: interaction models (V–M, N–M) numeric formulas or normative references
+- TODO-SE6: collect benchmark numerical examples and attach normative sources
+
+References
+- NTC2018 §7.2 (where available) — use as primary; fallback to EC2/EC1/EC8 documented where NTC omits specifics.
+

